      <memberdef kind="function" id="classcsmp_1_1_brittle_failure_visitor_1a23f93dab10d3970cd4229b22691d1201" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void csmp::BrittleFailureVisitor&lt; dim &gt;::Visit</definition>
        <argsstring>(Element&lt; dim &gt; *)</argsstring>
        <name>Visit</name>
        <qualifiedname>csmp::BrittleFailureVisitor::Visit</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="classcsmp_1_1_visitor_1a1a3ed57d253eef9a0097232c7359627c">Visit</reimplements>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_element" kindref="compound">Element</ref>&lt; dim &gt; *</type>
          <defname>e</defname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Loops over the element integration points and evaluates shear and tensile failure potential. Where failure occurred the variable &apos;failure&apos; is set to 1. A distinction is made between tensile &apos;tensile failure&apos; and shear failure &apos;failure&apos; variables.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>it is assumed that the tensile strength is about 1/10 of the cohesive strength of the rock</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>SKM 28/9/2014 - added case where stress is placed on the element. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
